    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers on **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.72), our clear top-tier plays. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a lucrative matchup against the soft-tossing Quintana (5.24 xERA), and his promotion to the #3 hole combined with a favorable platoon edge makes him our anchor. Meanwhile, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a plug-and-play stud despite the modest SP skill adjustment; his ability to drive production in all five categories mitigates any risk posed by Painter. **Daulton Varsho** (67.26) and **Taylor Ward** (66.35) also grade out as elite starting options today, largely due to strong park factors and advantageous platoon splits against their respective right-handed matchups.\n\nOur most difficult benching decision involved **Matt Chapman**, who fell just short of the 60-point threshold at 55.56. While he holds a decent projection, the combination of a left-handed matchup against Schultz and the fact that he is currently nullifying our team\u2019s stolen base ceiling pushed him out of the starting frame in favor of higher-efficiency hitters. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Jeremiah Jackson** (52.61); while his raw score is marginal, the 100% stolen base opportunity window against Valdez, F makes him a vital \"speed-chase\" play that warrants inclusion despite a sub-optimal #8 lineup position.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the current state of our roster. We are navigating significant depth issues with **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler** all currently unavailable due to injury or rest, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active utility players. We are also keeping a close watch on **Jonathan Aranda** (44.24), whose score is suppressed by a negative wind factor and a tough platoon disadvantage against Weathers. If the wind shifts or late lineup changes bump **Jonathan Aranda** or **Bryson Stott** further down the order, 